<title>NEW ZEALAND: PDL half year profit slips 6.5 pct.</title>
<headline>PDL half year profit slips 6.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half yr result to Sep 30</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   7.04 vs 7.53</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 41.1 vs 55.4</p>
<p>    Div (cents)				 20.0 vs 27.0</p>
<p>    Turnover				   170.6 vs 154.6</p>
<p>    Pretax profit				7.6 vs 11.9</p>
<p>    Tax					    2.0 vs 3.7</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		   credit 1.5 vs nil</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	 13.37 vs 13.15</p>
<p>Dividend carries 9.851 cps imputation credit.</p>
<p>Pay date Dec 13</p>
<p>Reg date Dec 6</p>
<p>Ex div   Dec 9</p>
<p>Note - PDL Holdings is a plastics and electronics manufacturer. PDL said it was acquiring the remaining 39 percent of the shares it does not already own in Mastertrade Group Ltd. As at September 30, it had acquired 37.15 percent, resulting in a net gain of NZ$1.643 million on the acquisition. Restructuring costs totalled NZ$184,000, bringing the total extraordinaries credit to NZ$1.459 million.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
